RETRO = '  <section id="apwh-build-20260804-20260921"><h2>APWH, August 4 to September 21: 47.9 days from taking the course to a dark-published course at the hosted QC ceiling</h2>\n    <p>Evidence window: 2026-08-04T07:29Z (the first written ownership claim) to 2026-09-21T05:10Z (the cut of the course record). Course: AP World History, native TimeBack course <code>ap-world-history-native-202608-v1</code>, published dark. Every number below is copied from <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#where-the-days-went">the APWH FINDINGS record on the course repository\'s main branch</a>, which links each claim to its receipt. This entry names mechanisms, not people. <a href="lessons.html#apwh-lessons-20260921">Lessons into practice</a>.</p>\n    <h3>Where the days went</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li><b>Period 0, Inherited baseline (the factory\'s build lane) (2026-07-27 to 08-04, 7.7 days).</b> Moved: the repository, the oracle and the only committed Faultless Bar run (status fail). Waited: organization CI billing lapsed, so merged did not mean deployed; STATUS.md froze on 07-30. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#0-inherited-baseline-factory-build-lane-2026-07-27t1538z-to-2026-08-04t0729z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 1, Taking the course: access, instruments, measurement layer (2026-08-04 to 08-16, 12.7 days).</b> Moved: credentials in 0.4 days; write access on 08-09; the measurement layer repaired first; 33 autopilot pull requests in 23.2 hours. Waited: hand-offs to the old platform route; 71 gates returned 404; the first paid judge sweep halted because all 933 items failed the structural gate. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#1-taking-the-course-access-instruments-measurement-layer-2026-08-04t0729z-to-2026-08-16t2359z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 2, Bank repair behind the shared pool; acceptance instrument named (2026-08-17 to 08-21, 5.0 days).</b> Moved: rationale and tagging repairs; the Faultless Bar named and made runnable from a pushed ref. Waited: 15.0 and 8.2 hours for the shared factory pool; a placement held 9.4 days. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#2-bank-repair-behind-the-shared-pool-acceptance-instrument-named-2026-08-17t0000z-to-2026-08-21t2359z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 3, Local gates, grading hold, deficit audit (2026-08-22 to 08-28, 6.5 days).</b> Moved: the frozen blueprint corrected after 28.4 days; all 123 grading calls settled; the course profile landed on the platform. Waited: a local six-gate contract held 4.9 days and was retired; a 66.4-hour hold ruled unnecessary; no platform landing for 8.7 days. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#3-local-gates-grading-hold-deficit-audit-2026-08-22t0000z-to-2026-08-28t1259z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 4, Platform pivot and runbook phases 0 to 2 (2026-08-28 to 09-02, 4.6 days).</b> Moved: the target became TimeBack-direct; a publisher in 4.2 hours; 71 of 71 gates verified; four lessons live in 2.9 hours. Waited: owner-word holds of 5.2 to 7.6 hours; a 22.1-hour wall on one PR; a 10.7-hour merge-gate stop on rows red on main. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#4-platform-pivot-and-runbook-phases-0-to-2-2026-08-28t1259z-to-2026-09-02t0434z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 5, Gate repair, stimulus bank, bank gates (2026-09-02 to 09-08, 6.2 days).</b> Moved: 422 served gate items with no judge verdict found and repaired in about 30 hours; the mock rebuilt to the exam\'s shape. Waited: one pull request sat 75 hours as a draft; three decisions filed with no deadline. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#5-gate-repair-stimulus-bank-bank-gates-2026-09-02t0434z-to-2026-09-08t0836z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 6, Course Builder built; APWH waits (2026-09-08 to 09-17, 8.9 days).</b> Moved: the Course Builder built and took APWH through step 1 and the write layer; the Phase 6 operators merged. Waited: seven days with no APWH landing while HumGeo landed on the shared seat; the event feed dropped rows for 11 days; 14.8 hours from push to merge on PR #1167. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#6-course-builder-built-apwh-waits-2026-09-08t0836z-to-2026-09-17t0608z">Period record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Period 7, Publish dark, waves, regression, rulings, QC climb (2026-09-17 to 09-21, 4.0 days).</b> Moved: published dark in 3.7 hours; a 6,281-row activity wave; hosted QC from 0.5586 to 0.9843 in 17.2 hours; 16 platform merges. Waited: live rewrites broke the source envelope (four re-pins in 9.4 hours); a QC regression undone; 13.75 hours from a Mac restart to the re-bind; enrollment, walk and activation not done. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#7-publish-dark-waves-regression-rulings-qc-climb-2026-09-17t0608z-to-2026-09-21t0510z">Period record</a>.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>Periods 1 to 7 sum to 47.9 days; period 0 is the 7.7-day inherited baseline. Two lanes ran at once in periods 2, 3, 6 and 7. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#where-the-days-went">Where the days went</a>.</p>\n    <h3>What landed</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li><b>A course published dark through the installed Course Builder</b> on 09-17 (run 9, release .52): 176 lessons in 9 units, 176 formatted article pages, 880 static check documents, 71 topic mastery gates, unit forms and a two-section mock exam. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#7-publish-dark-waves-regression-rulings-qc-climb-2026-09-17t0608z-to-2026-09-21t0510z">Period 7</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Hosted Course QC from 0.5586 to 0.9843 in 17.2 hours</b> over nine runs, at a measured ceiling of 0.9847; 3,480 live item rewrites with readback and zero-write replay across 21 waves. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#hosted-course-qc-run-by-run">Run-by-run table</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Four platform landings carry the live course:</b> ap-one PRs #1167 (Phase 6 operators), #1185 (activity waves and lesson shape), #1189 (QC climb operators) and #1188 (player-safe check XML). <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#baseline-and-reporting-identity">Baseline and reporting identity</a>.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>What failed, why, and the correction that worked</h3>\n    <p>Thirteen causes cut across the periods; they overlap in time, so their day counts do not add. Each links to its cause section, which ends in the one change for the next build. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#why-it-took-this-long-cross-cutting-causes">All thirteen</a>.</p>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li><b>C1. The publication target moved twice.</b> The student platform target changed 31.9 days in (to TimeBack-direct) and again on 09-18 (everything in AP One, same shape). Two intake waits of 19.4 and 18.0 days closed within a day of the first ruling. Correction: Name the student destination and the full object inventory in the course profile before the first hand-off; when the close bar sits in another team\'s write corridor, file the fallback route in the same issue. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c1-the-publication-target-moved-twice">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C2. The instruments could not read the course.</b> The acceptance runner imported code that lived on one machine, the paid judge would not read items until a structural gate all 933 failed was cleared, and 422 served gate items carried no verdict for 36 days. The hosted reader\'s rules (one-article context, iframe pages, per-component ordering, a record-size failure that dropped every report email) were learned from paid scores. Correction: Run the acceptance instrument from a pushed ref on a 200-question slice in the first week; read checks.py and timeback_reader.py before any structural write; carry the reader\'s known needs from the first publish. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c2-the-instruments-could-not-read-the-course">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C3. One shared pool, seat, lock and install, with a serial course order.</b> One factory pool, one seat, one writer lock and one Course Builder install served HumGeo first by ruling. Measured waits: 15.0 and 8.2 hours on the pool; seven days with 10 APWH rows against 137 HumGeo rows. Correction: Give each course its own controller lease, lock locator and install root; measure the queue place before every paid step and write the wait into the ETA. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c3-one-shared-pool-one-shared-seat-one-shared-lock-and-one-shared-install-with-a-serial-course-order">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C4. Owner-word freshness gates and per-step holds.</b> The PR-open and merge hooks wanted an owner quote younger than two hours, and grants were scoped to the transcript they were typed in. Finished work waited 5.2 to 29.5 hours for a morning word. Correction: Standing authority until the course is live, recorded once in a grant file every window reads; gates still run; no clock on the owner\'s words; an open decision blocks the publish step or carries a typed default. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c4-owner-word-freshness-gates-and-per-step-holds">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C5. Local gates stricter than the factory\'s.</b> A six-gate contract, an executor no-progress latch and a merge gate that refused on suite rows already red on main added holds the factory did not ask for: 4.9 days of vocabulary, a 66.4-hour hold ruled unnecessary, 10.7 hours on one PR. Correction: State progress only in the publication runbook\'s phase names; every local gate runs in shadow except the certification gate; a base-red suite gets an adjudication row, not a refusal. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c5-local-gates-stricter-than-the-factorys">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C6. Live rewrites broke the source envelope.</b> The producer hashes every item, so each live item wave broke the source envelope and needed a source re-pin plus a full republish (about 2,300 writes and 65 minutes). Four re-pins landed between 01:08Z and 10:32Z on 2026-09-18 (9.4 hours by subtraction, as the period 7 record states); 3,480 rewrites were unfolded at the cut. Correction: Make the re-pin a step of the item-campaign operator (plan, seal, execute, replay, re-pin) and keep the publisher\'s checkpoint in the repository so a re-pin republishes only what changed. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c6-live-rewrites-broke-the-source-envelope">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C7. The measurement layer was wrong or stale.</b> A report header frozen for 10.9 days, a stale branch that turned MISSING into PASS, stale-clone counts, a false \'24 tests broken\' claim, an event feed that dropped rows for 11 days, and a status view that hid three weeks of landed work. Correction: Re-derive every quoted number from the live remote in the same turn; assert that a regenerated report changed; pair every hold with a \'landed so far\' line; point the event log at a receiver that exists. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c7-the-measurement-layer-was-wrong-or-stale">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C8. Review ceremony, capped review lanes and a tight CI budget.</b> Six or seven review rounds on one PR, two capped rounds with no verdict, a draft PR that sat 75.4 hours outside merge policy, CI timeouts on a forked pool, and out-of-GitHub rounds nobody could count. Correction: Every review finding returns with a deterministic, tested fix; a capped lane writes its report file first; PRs post ready-for-review; a small-course fixture keeps the suite under the CI cap; out-of-GitHub rounds are linked from the PR. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c8-review-ceremony-capped-review-lanes-and-a-tight-ci-budget">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C9. The publication contract arrived after the content.</b> The 910-line runbook was handed over on 08-28 and never committed; on 09-08 the native pipeline stopped at Phase 2. The Phase 6 operators merged 17.0 days after Phase 2 pricing, and one plan needed five versions in a day because version 1 assumed modules that did not exist. Correction: Commit the publication runbook and a per-phase module inventory (exists or missing) to the course repository on intake day; plan from that inventory, never from an assumed pipeline. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c9-the-publication-contract-arrived-after-the-content">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C10. Shared tooling replaced; processes that died with their terminal or machine.</b> A publish run died with its shell; a Mac restart killed the after-wave chain (13.75 hours from restart to re-bind); another lane installed a release over this lane\'s build; a full disk stopped every tool. Correction: Run every unattended chain detached with progress visible from its checkpoint; refusal identity includes release and operator bytes with a retry budget; one install root per lane; free-space preflight before any sealed execute. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c10-shared-tooling-replaced-and-processes-that-died-with-their-terminal-or-machine">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C11. Changes made and then undone.</b> A Gate 2 hold ruled unnecessary, 71 gate links undone after a QC drop from 0.878 to 0.584, a practice fold undone the same day, a lesson-shape ruling withdrawn within the hour, and a wave excluded on a stale hash then re-landed. Correction: Pilot one lesson, verify on the rendered course and one QC read, then scale; keep the operator\'s undo ready; a step that needs evidence the factory does not hold is ruled at the plan stage, not held. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c11-changes-made-and-then-undone">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C12. The content bar moved late.</b> \'No demo before student-ready\' (07-28), \'the mock should be the same as the actual exam\' (09-03, 2,172 items retired), test-likeness (08-31), video first and formatted articles (09-20) each arrived after content built to the earlier bar. Correction: Write the content bar (exam shape of the mock, stimulus share, lesson row order, article format) into the course profile before generation, and show the owner one rendered lesson before the bank is generated. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c12-the-content-bar-moved-late">Cause record</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>C13. Decisions and work orders with no deadline and no closing owner.</b> Three decisions filed on 09-08 sat 13 days; work orders #9, #10, #12 and #46 went silent for 38 to 41 days; one intake closed while its destination stayed open. Correction: Every decision row carries a deadline and a default; every work order names a closing owner; superseded destinations close with a pointer the day the route changes. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#c13-decisions-and-work-orders-with-no-deadline-and-no-closing-owner">Cause record</a>.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>What remains open</h3>\n    <ul class="work-list">\n      <li>Enrollment, the walk as a student, activation and the release flip have not run; the course is <code>publishStatus</code> testing. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#open-items-at-2026-09-21t0510z">Open items</a>.</li>\n      <li>3,480 live item rewrites are not yet folded into the committed source; the course verifier reads them as drift until a re-pin lands.</li>\n      <li>Two hosted QC service defects (job record size with no report email; the ordering check\'s per-component rule) and one video service filing are open.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>How the next course reuses this</h3>\n    <p>The record closes with 57 lessons, each bound to a Course Builder step or gate; the ones the pages did not yet carry are folded into <a href="lessons.html#apwh-lessons-20260921">the lessons entry of the same date</a> and into spec rules R9. The shortest version: name the destination, the object inventory and the content bar in the course profile before the first hand-off; run the acceptance instrument and one small hosted QC job from a pushed ref in week one; commit the runbook and a module inventory at intake; record owner authority once with no clock; give each course its own lane, lock and install; and re-pin the source as part of every live wave. <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">The 57 lessons</a>.</p>\n  </section>\n'

LESSONS = '    <section id="apwh-lessons-20260921"><h2>August 4 to September 21: what the APWH build teaches the next course build</h2>\n      <p>Source: the APWH build (<a href="retro.html#apwh-build-20260804-20260921">retrospective</a>) and its <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">57-lesson table</a> on the course repository\'s main branch. This entry carries only the rules the pages did not yet state: 25 new rules, 27 amendments to rules already here in a HumGeo-only or partial form, and 2 period lessons outside the table. Each names the Course Builder step it binds to and links its receipt; the table row and the period section hold the measured numbers.</p>\n      <h3>New rules</h3>\n      <ul class="work-list">\n        <li id="apwh-content-bar-first-20260921"><b>Fix the content bar (mock shape, stimulus share, practice cap) in the course profile before the bank is generated.</b> On APWH the mock ruling arrived on day 38 and retired 2,172 items. <i>Builder step:</i> content step (p3 bank gates). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L3</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-5">period 5</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-instrument-pushed-ref-20260921"><b>The acceptance instrument (the Faultless Bar) must run from a pushed ref before any content work depends on its verdicts; the step 1 oracle gate fails closed when it does not.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> step 1 oracle gate / p5 cold QC. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L5</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-2">period 2</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-read-reader-first-20260921"><b>Read the hosted QC reader\'s code (checks.py, timeback_reader.py) and run one small hosted job before any structural write; ship the hidden article-text block, static check XML and the stimulus in every judge payload from the first publish.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p6 cold QC (pre-write reader check). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L8</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-judge-native-course-20260921"><b>Once a namespace publish exists, cold QC judges the native course id, never the source course id.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p6 cold QC (release .53). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L9</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-qc-cache-is-instrument-20260921"><b>The hosted verdict cache is part of the instrument: its key is prompt version, course, question and lesson context, with no cold flag; above about 2,000 items the job record reads FAILED and no email is sent, so the loop polls on report presence.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L10</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-read-fatal-codes-first-20260921"><b>Read the stored fatal codes before any paid re-judge; never call the judge poster with an empty slot file, because it judges the whole pool.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L14</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-own-defect-classes-20260921"><b>Name the course\'s own defect classes from its own bytes before reusing another course\'s scanner; a fixed-string class gets a free scanner before any model critic; a zero from a filter needs a positive control.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> census step before any campaign. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L15</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-5">period 5</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-fold-and-repin-per-wave-20260921"><b>Budget a source fold and re-pin beside every live item wave; a live rewrite breaks the publication envelope, so each wave needs a source landing plus a republish (about 2,300 writes, about 65 minutes on APWH).</b> <i>Builder step:</i> item campaign, land step (re-pin). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L16</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-repin-same-pr-20260921"><b>Any write-activity change lands with the source re-pin in the same pull request, or CI is red whatever the content; every course ships a re-pin script.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> land step (release .37 re-pin). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L17</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-census-ids-before-embed-20260921"><b>Census live ids before any operator embeds items by id; normalize static check XML before publishing it as an asset; verify rendering with a browser click-through against a live hybrid article.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> p6 article pages. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L18</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-standing-authority-20260921"><b>Owner grants are standing authority until the course is live, recorded once in a grant file every window reads; every gate still runs; no clock on the owner\'s words.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> land step (PR-open and merge hooks). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L24</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-local-gates-shadow-20260921"><b>Local gates are never stronger than the factory\'s, the certification gate excepted; every local gate runs in shadow; progress is stated only in the runbook\'s phase names.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> every local gate (shadow mode). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L25</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-3">period 3</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-ci-budget-20260921"><b>Budget platform CI: the suite uses most of the 25-minute cap; never fork a process pool inside an xdist worker; use a small-course fixture; test under CI\'s Python version before pushing.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> land step (CI). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L29</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-shared-install-20260921"><b>A shared Course Builder install is one surface: land on main first, message the other lane with the sha, never install a branch build into the shared root.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> install step. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L30</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-fan-out-20260921"><b>Fan out content lanes (videos, articles, items, FRQs) as parallel shards; scripts and per-item files before agents; every workflow agent carries a fixed-task line.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> content lanes. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L32</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-fallback-in-same-issue-20260921"><b>When the close bar sits in another team\'s write corridor, file the fallback route in the same issue; ask for the capability, not the token; check a fork is current before declaring code unreachable.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> intake filing. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L34</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-1">period 1</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-landed-so-far-20260921"><b>Every status view pairs the current hold with a \'landed so far\' line fed from receipts; the event log points at a receiver that exists, and a dispatch nobody receives is an error.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> status pages, event log. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L42</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-security-disposition-20260921"><b>A high-severity automated security finding at merge time gets a written disposition on the pull request before the merge.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> land step (merge gate row). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L44</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-link-review-rounds-20260921"><b>Link every out-of-GitHub review round from the pull request so wait and rework are countable.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> land step (PR body). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L45</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-blueprint-reconcile-20260921"><b>A frozen blueprint is still a document with errors: reconcile it against the authoritative rubric in week one and register a measurable oracle predicate for every requirement at the start.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> step 1 oracle gate. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L47</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-3">period 3</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-qa-terms-20260921"><b>Describe QA work in QA terms; write worker prompts through the codex-prompt skill with the shortest read path; owner asks are two plain sentences.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> review brief; step cards. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L49</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-defer-nothing-20260921"><b>Defer nothing: no deferred findings in a pull request; a plan date is an intent, not a state.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> land step (admitted-gap scan). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L50</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-5">period 5</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-option-count-20260921"><b>Mock forms carry the real exam\'s option count and everything else carries four; the count is read from the course profile, never converted after generation.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> course profile (p0): mock option count read from the exam; item emit rules. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L55</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-4">period 4</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-no-licensed-articles-20260921"><b>Articles from a source that needs a license are excluded; the course writes its own; a provenance scan runs before any outside body enters a keep or import column.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> article step (p2): provenance scan before any import. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L56</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-contributor-not-owner-20260921"><b>A contributor\'s activity on a course repository is a coordination fact, never ownership or permission; ownership is read from the profile and the remote at intake.</b> <i>Builder step:</i> intake step (p0): ownership read from the profile and the remote; contributor activity as a one-writer coordination row. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L57</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-3">period 3</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-cap-at-factory-bounds-20260921"><b>Cap attempts at the factory\'s own bounds, then rebuild.</b> one tagging pass per item ended a retry loop; an exhaustion receipt ended a re-post loop that spent about 75 candidates for 0 accepted. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-and-judge loop round cap; needs-human ledger. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-2">period 2 lessons</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-rule-at-plan-stage-20260921"><b>Rule at the plan stage on any step whose evidence the factory does not hold; never hold on it.</b> The grader-evidence hold ran 66.4 hours for receipts the factory does not produce. <i>Builder step:</i> plan step; needs-human ledger. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-3">period 3 lessons</a>.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Amendments to rules already on this page</h3>\n      <p>Each names the section that carries the HumGeo or partial form, then the part APWH adds.</p>\n      <ul class="work-list">\n        <li id="apwh-destination-first-20260921"><b>Name the student destination and every object kind (videos, practice, checks, mock, writing, XP) in the course profile before the first hand-off.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 1 (confirm the shipping route). APWH adds: the full object inventory in the course profile before the first hand-off, and the fallback route. <i>Builder step:</i> course profile (p0). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L1</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build">period 0</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-publish-whole-shape-20260921"><b>Publish the whole shape and diff source against live, object by object, before calling publish done.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#humgeo-postassembly-20260916">humgeo-postassembly-20260916</a> (refresh the finished composition). APWH adds: a pre-publish diff of the source package against the live tree, object by object, and the rule that an open decision blocks the publish step or carries a typed default. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 publish dark (pre-publish inventory diff). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L2</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-lesson-shape-two-readers-20260921"><b>Decide the lesson shape with both the student player and the QC reader in view; never reshape the live course for a reader.</b> Already here: <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (video shape repair: rows read Video and Reading). APWH adds: the player renders one row per component, so folding activities hides them; never reshape the live course for a QC reader; file the reader gap instead. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 lesson shape. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L4</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-structural-before-judge-20260921"><b>Run the structural prerequisites (rationales, skill codes) before any paid judge sweep; the order is generate, tag, rationales, verdict, bank.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, dispatch card (free checks pass before spending). APWH adds: the fixed order: generate, tag, write rationales, get the factory verdict, then bank; a structural pre-check ahead of any paid judge sweep. <i>Builder step:</i> content step, structural pre-check before judge. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L6</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-1">period 1</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-served-needs-verdict-20260921"><b>Every served item carries a factory judge verdict on its served bytes; the bank gate refuses one without it.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "What changed" (a receipt must identify the exact bytes it judges; green mechanics are necessary, not sufficient). APWH adds: the bank gate refuses any served item without a stored factory judge verdict on its served bytes; a pipeline-invariant label is not a judgment. <i>Builder step:</i> p3 bank gates. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L7</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-5">period 5</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-ceiling-whole-population-20260921"><b>Measure the whole item population before quoting a ceiling; a gate-only score hides the largest class.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (compute the QC ceiling before chasing the score). APWH adds: measure every population before quoting a ceiling: a gate-only score of 0.878 on 1,988 items hid 2,136 PowerPath-100 fails. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 QC loop (split step). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L12</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-fails-feed-next-round-20260921"><b>Judge fails feed the next generation at once; stop redrafting a code that returns no reasoning after a zero-pass round.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, retry card (diagnose the premise before another attempt). APWH adds: judge fails feed the next generation at once with the fatal codes and the target EK; when S8 (content accuracy, returned with no reasoning) is the only code left, stop after a round with zero passes. <i>Builder step:</i> draft-judge loop. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L13</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-video-first-formatted-articles-20260921"><b>Video comes first in every lesson; articles carry headings, bold key ideas and a table or figure; a producer rejection is not a content verdict.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#design-assumption-article-coverage-20260912">design-assumption-article-coverage-20260912</a> (verify assumptions inherited from the original design); <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (video shape repair). APWH adds: video first in every lesson; articles with headings, bold key ideas and a table or figure; \'rejected by producer QC\' is not \'bad article\'. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 lesson shape; article gate. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L20</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-detached-and-rebind-20260921"><b>Run every unattended publish detached; re-bind on a recut mismatch instead of stopping; shard operators at about 400 rows.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#humgeo-postassembly-20260916">humgeo-postassembly-20260916</a> (preserve partial progress); <a href="lessons.html#native-terminal-receipts-20260914">native-terminal-receipts-20260914</a> (recovery: reattach, never restart). APWH adds: run unattended publishes detached with progress visible from the checkpoint; refusal identity includes release and operator bytes with a retry budget; re-bind rather than stop on a recut mismatch; shard at about 400 rows; stale-lock recovery. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 publish (materialize, re-bind). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L21</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-profile-before-asking-20260921"><b>Every step reads the committed factory profile at live main before it may ask the owner anything.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Factory-canonical operating rules" (read the committed factory contract before acting); <a href="lessons.html#coverage-first-builder-20260910">coverage-first-builder-20260910</a> (decision requests state the authorized default). APWH adds: a step refuses to ask the owner until each field cites a live-main read of the committed profile. <i>Builder step:</i> every step card (resolve_from). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L22</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-live-facts-become-rules-20260921"><b>A platform fact learned live becomes a builder rule the same day; the next course reads the list before its first live write.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#humgeo-postassembly-20260916">humgeo-postassembly-20260916</a> (test the address and the stored result). APWH adds: the general rule: each platform fact learned live becomes a builder rule the first time it is measured, and the next course reads the rule list before its first live write. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 publish (releases .49 to .57). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L23</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-landing-floor-20260921"><b>Keep the landing ceremony at its floor: two review rounds at most, no drafts, no merge before the BFF check finishes, recover a capped report from disk.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#review-28-rounds">review-28-rounds</a> (one round is the target); <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (bind the review receipt to the exact head). APWH adds: never merge before the BFF check finishes; post ready-for-review, never a draft (PR #992 sat 75.4 hours); recover a capped lane\'s report from disk before spending a round. <i>Builder step:</i> land step (review, merge gate). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L26</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-5">period 5</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-deterministic-fix-20260921"><b>Every review finding carries a tested, deterministic, class-closing fix; a validator is one total rule with a mutation test.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#review-28-rounds">review-28-rounds</a> (class-close receipt). APWH adds: every review finding returns with a deterministic, tested, class-closing fix; a validator is one total rule with a mutation test; the author probes every guard before review. <i>Builder step:</i> land step (one-round-review). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L27</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-deadline-and-default-20260921"><b>Every decision row carries a deadline and a default; every work order names a closing owner; a superseded destination closes with a pointer the day the route changes.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#coverage-first-builder-20260910">coverage-first-builder-20260910</a> (decision requests state the authorized default and its cost). APWH adds: a deadline on every decision row; a closing owner on every work order; a superseded destination closes with a pointer the day the route changes. <i>Builder step:</i> needs-human ledger. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L33</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-1">period 1</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-queue-place-first-20260921"><b>Measure the queue place on the shared pool before every paid step and write the wait into the estimate; each course gets its own controller lease and lock.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, report card (an ETA has a reconciled dependency chain and duration evidence). APWH adds: measure the queue place on the shared factory pool before every paid step; give each course its own controller lease and lock; price the wait into the ETA. <i>Builder step:</i> campaign dispatch (slot filler). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L35</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-2">period 2</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-measurement-layer-first-20260921"><b>Repair the measurement layer on intake day: a committed report is a claim, a regenerated report must be shown to have changed, and MISSING never becomes PASS.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 6 (bind freshness to live remote state). APWH adds: a self-regenerating report needs an assertion that the regeneration hit; a MISSING exit is never turned into a PASS; the measurement layer is repaired on intake day before content work. <i>Builder step:</i> step 1 oracle gate. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L36</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-1">period 1</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-zero-needs-control-20260921"><b>A zero returned by a filter is not evidence until a positive control shows the filter can hit.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 6 (bind freshness to live remote state); <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, report card (UNMEASURED). APWH adds: a zero from a filter needs a positive control. <i>Builder step:</i> every step (freshness re-earn). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L37</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-4">period 4</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-premise-on-bytes-20260921"><b>Check the recorded diagnosis and the spec premise against bytes before building the fix.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, retry card (diagnose the premise before another attempt). APWH adds: check a recorded diagnosis and a spec\'s premise against bytes before building the fix, at the plan stage and not only after a failed retry. <i>Builder step:</i> campaign plan (phase 0 measure). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L38</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-5">period 5</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-false-absence-ladder-20260921"><b>Read the factory\'s answer from bytes first; walk the false-absence ladder before declaring a tool missing.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Factory-canonical operating rules" (read the committed factory contract before acting; file the gap). APWH adds: a fix with no file path is an invention; check the git remote before calling a tool the factory\'s; walk the false-absence ladder (organization list, fresh fetch, conformance receipts, catalog) before declaring a tool missing. <i>Builder step:</i> every step (factory prescription first). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L39</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-2">period 2</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-precedent-before-asking-20260921"><b>Never present a mechanism choice to the owner when a live course holds the precedent; a named blocker needs an exhaustion receipt.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Factory-canonical operating rules" (approvals are scoped); <a href="lessons.html#coverage-first-builder-20260910">coverage-first-builder-20260910</a> (decision requests). APWH adds: never present a mechanism choice when live courses hold a precedent; a named blocker needs an exhaustion receipt; a block word needs a machinery check first. <i>Builder step:</i> needs-human ledger (gate before a row is written). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L40</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-2">period 2</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-full-bodies-at-capture-20260921"><b>Persist full request and response bodies at capture; bind the consumer contract before spend; never re-judge a deterministic fail.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, retry card (preserve the full response). APWH adds: bind the downstream consumer contract before spend; never re-judge a deterministic fail. <i>Builder step:</i> campaign capture. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L41</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-3">period 3</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-size-from-batches-20260921"><b>Size paid checks from recorded per-batch durations; outward estimates use the cautious end.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910">morning-retro-20260910</a>, report card (ETA needs duration evidence or reads UNMEASURED). APWH adds: size paid checks from a real run\'s per-batch durations, never from the run span divided by the record count; outward ETAs use the cautious end. <i>Builder step:</i> plan / ETA. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L43</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-2">period 2</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-file-mismatch-day-one-20260921"><b>File instrument-contract mismatches on day one with a reproduction; keep acceptance evidence in a repository that will not be recreated.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (commit the receipts you cite); <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (uncommitted receipts are not evidence). APWH adds: file instrument-contract mismatches on day one with a reproduction, because they do not close by re-running; keep acceptance evidence in a repository that will not be recreated. <i>Builder step:</i> intake filing; evidence store. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L46</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-4">period 4</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-never-freeze-factory-20260921"><b>Never freeze an expectation of factory behavior; suspect our own environment before calling another repository\'s tests broken.</b> Already here: lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 2 (prefer measured live state); <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (base-red suites need an adjudication). APWH adds: never freeze an expectation of factory behavior; in-place edits of factory artifacts reproduce the writer byte for byte; suspect our environment before calling another repository\'s tests broken. <i>Builder step:</i> campaign runner; landing staging. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L51</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-4">period 4</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-commit-runbook-at-intake-20260921"><b>Commit the status file, the publication runbook and a per-phase module inventory to the course repository at intake.</b> Already here: <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (uncommitted receipts are not evidence). APWH adds: commit the status file, the publication runbook and a per-phase module inventory to the course repository at intake; the record must not stop at handoff. <i>Builder step:</i> intake step. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L52</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-6">period 6</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-wait-not-rounds-20260921"><b>The lever on elapsed time is the wait between landings, not the review round count.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#review-28-rounds">review-28-rounds</a> (one round is the target). APWH adds: the qualification: the lever is the wait between landings, not the round count; on APWH two capped rounds still yielded 11 findings while 3.1- and 5.1-day silences cost more. <i>Builder step:</i> land step. Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L53</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n        <li id="apwh-video-queue-first-20260921"><b>Before a render wave, read the video service\'s queue for the shared principal and clear stale rows; budget against the service\'s measured state.</b> Already here: <a href="lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920">publish-faster-20260920</a> (a 202 from the video service means queued); <a href="retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920">humgeo-closeout-20260920</a> (video service out of disk). APWH adds: read the video service\'s queue for the shared principal and clear stale rows before a render wave; the unfinished-video cap is not exposed by the API; a full service disk turns every cancel into HTTP 500. <i>Builder step:</i> p6 video lane (pre-render check). Receipt: <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-to-build-into-the-next-course-build">L54</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ilmych/apwh-blueprint-build/blob/df018cc961320bcfa512debdfcfbe2ae9e4a39c9/FINDINGS.md#what-this-period-teaches-the-next-build-7">period 7</a>.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Present already, no new entry: L11 and L12\'s loop (publish-faster-20260920), L19 (publish-faster-20260920), L28 (publish-faster-20260920), L31 (publish-faster-20260920), L48 (humgeo-run-20260909). Full verdict table: the coverage file beside the course record\'s fold.</p>\n    </section>\n'

SPEC_ADD = '### R9. Rules learned on APWH (2026-08-04 to 09-21)\n\n- R9.1 Name the student destination and every object kind (videos, practice, checks, mock, writing, XP) in the course profile before the first hand-off. (L1; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 1)\n- R9.2 Publish the whole shape and diff source against live, object by object, before calling publish done. (L2; amends lessons.html#humgeo-postassembly-20260916)\n- R9.3 Fix the content bar (mock shape, stimulus share, practice cap) in the course profile before the bank is generated. On APWH the mock ruling arrived on day 38 and retired 2,172 items. (L3)\n- R9.4 Decide the lesson shape with both the student player and the QC reader in view; never reshape the live course for a reader. (L4; amends retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920)\n- R9.5 The acceptance instrument (the Faultless Bar) must run from a pushed ref before any content work depends on its verdicts; the step 1 oracle gate fails closed when it does not. (L5)\n- R9.6 Run the structural prerequisites (rationales, skill codes) before any paid judge sweep; the order is generate, tag, rationales, verdict, bank. (L6; amends lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910, dispatch card)\n- R9.7 Every served item carries a factory judge verdict on its served bytes; the bank gate refuses one without it. (L7; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "What changed")\n- R9.8 Read the hosted QC reader\'s code (checks.py, timeback_reader.py) and run one small hosted job before any structural write; ship the hidden article-text block, static check XML and the stimulus in every judge payload from the first publish. (L8)\n- R9.9 Once a namespace publish exists, cold QC judges the native course id, never the source course id. (L9)\n- R9.10 The hosted verdict cache is part of the instrument: its key is prompt version, course, question and lesson context, with no cold flag; above about 2,000 items the job record reads FAILED and no email is sent, so the loop polls on report presence. (L10)\n- R9.11 Measure the whole item population before quoting a ceiling; a gate-only score hides the largest class. (L12; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R9.12 Judge fails feed the next generation at once; stop redrafting a code that returns no reasoning after a zero-pass round. (L13; amends lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910, retry card)\n- R9.13 Read the stored fatal codes before any paid re-judge; never call the judge poster with an empty slot file, because it judges the whole pool. (L14)\n- R9.14 Name the course\'s own defect classes from its own bytes before reusing another course\'s scanner; a fixed-string class gets a free scanner before any model critic; a zero from a filter needs a positive control. (L15)\n- R9.15 Budget a source fold and re-pin beside every live item wave; a live rewrite breaks the publication envelope, so each wave needs a source landing plus a republish (about 2,300 writes, about 65 minutes on APWH). (L16)\n- R9.16 Any write-activity change lands with the source re-pin in the same pull request, or CI is red whatever the content; every course ships a re-pin script. (L17)\n- R9.17 Census live ids before any operator embeds items by id; normalize static check XML before publishing it as an asset; verify rendering with a browser click-through against a live hybrid article. (L18)\n- R9.18 Video comes first in every lesson; articles carry headings, bold key ideas and a table or figure; a producer rejection is not a content verdict. (L20; amends lessons.html#design-assumption-article-coverage-20260912)\n- R9.19 Run every unattended publish detached; re-bind on a recut mismatch instead of stopping; shard operators at about 400 rows. (L21; amends lessons.html#humgeo-postassembly-20260916)\n- R9.20 Every step reads the committed factory profile at live main before it may ask the owner anything. (L22; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Factory-canonical operating rules")\n- R9.21 A platform fact learned live becomes a builder rule the same day; the next course reads the list before its first live write. (L23; amends lessons.html#humgeo-postassembly-20260916)\n- R9.22 Owner grants are standing authority until the course is live, recorded once in a grant file every window reads; every gate still runs; no clock on the owner\'s words. (L24)\n- R9.23 Local gates are never stronger than the factory\'s, the certification gate excepted; every local gate runs in shadow; progress is stated only in the runbook\'s phase names. (L25)\n- R9.24 Keep the landing ceremony at its floor: two review rounds at most, no drafts, no merge before the BFF check finishes, recover a capped report from disk. (L26; amends lessons.html#review-28-rounds)\n- R9.25 Every review finding carries a tested, deterministic, class-closing fix; a validator is one total rule with a mutation test. (L27; amends lessons.html#review-28-rounds)\n- R9.26 Budget platform CI: the suite uses most of the 25-minute cap; never fork a process pool inside an xdist worker; use a small-course fixture; test under CI\'s Python version before pushing. (L29)\n- R9.27 A shared Course Builder install is one surface: land on main first, message the other lane with the sha, never install a branch build into the shared root. (L30)\n- R9.28 Fan out content lanes (videos, articles, items, FRQs) as parallel shards; scripts and per-item files before agents; every workflow agent carries a fixed-task line. (L32)\n- R9.29 Every decision row carries a deadline and a default; every work order names a closing owner; a superseded destination closes with a pointer the day the route changes. (L33; amends lessons.html#coverage-first-builder-20260910)\n- R9.30 When the close bar sits in another team\'s write corridor, file the fallback route in the same issue; ask for the capability, not the token; check a fork is current before declaring code unreachable. (L34)\n- R9.31 Measure the queue place on the shared pool before every paid step and write the wait into the estimate; each course gets its own controller lease and lock. (L35; amends lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910, report card)\n- R9.32 Repair the measurement layer on intake day: a committed report is a claim, a regenerated report must be shown to have changed, and MISSING never becomes PASS. (L36; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 6)\n- R9.33 A zero returned by a filter is not evidence until a positive control shows the filter can hit. (L37; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 6)\n- R9.34 Check the recorded diagnosis and the spec premise against bytes before building the fix. (L38; amends lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910, retry card)\n- R9.35 Read the factory\'s answer from bytes first; walk the false-absence ladder before declaring a tool missing. (L39; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Factory-canonical operating rules")\n- R9.36 Never present a mechanism choice to the owner when a live course holds the precedent; a named blocker needs an exhaustion receipt. (L40; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Factory-canonical operating rules")\n- R9.37 Persist full request and response bodies at capture; bind the consumer contract before spend; never re-judge a deterministic fail. (L41; amends lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910, retry card)\n- R9.38 Every status view pairs the current hold with a \'landed so far\' line fed from receipts; the event log points at a receiver that exists, and a dispatch nobody receives is an error. (L42)\n- R9.39 Size paid checks from recorded per-batch durations; outward estimates use the cautious end. (L43; amends lessons.html#morning-retro-20260910, report card)\n- R9.40 A high-severity automated security finding at merge time gets a written disposition on the pull request before the merge. (L44)\n- R9.41 Link every out-of-GitHub review round from the pull request so wait and rework are countable. (L45)\n- R9.42 File instrument-contract mismatches on day one with a reproduction; keep acceptance evidence in a repository that will not be recreated. (L46; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R9.43 A frozen blueprint is still a document with errors: reconcile it against the authoritative rubric in week one and register a measurable oracle predicate for every requirement at the start. (L47)\n- R9.44 Describe QA work in QA terms; write worker prompts through the codex-prompt skill with the shortest read path; owner asks are two plain sentences. (L49)\n- R9.45 Defer nothing: no deferred findings in a pull request; a plan date is an intent, not a state. (L50)\n- R9.46 Never freeze an expectation of factory behavior; suspect our own environment before calling another repository\'s tests broken. (L51; amends lessons.html, unanchored section "Lessons — the 24 hours after the Psych sync", item 2)\n- R9.47 Commit the status file, the publication runbook and a per-phase module inventory to the course repository at intake. (L52; amends retro.html#humgeo-closeout-20260920)\n- R9.48 The lever on elapsed time is the wait between landings, not the review round count. (L53; amends lessons.html#review-28-rounds)\n- R9.49 Before a render wave, read the video service\'s queue for the shared principal and clear stale rows; budget against the service\'s measured state. (L54; amends lessons.html#publish-faster-20260920)\n- R9.50 Mock forms carry the real exam\'s option count and everything else carries four; the count is read from the course profile, never converted after generation. (L55)\n- R9.51 Articles from a source that needs a license are excluded; the course writes its own; a provenance scan runs before any outside body enters a keep or import column. (L56)\n- R9.52 A contributor\'s activity on a course repository is a coordination fact, never ownership or permission; ownership is read from the profile and the remote at intake. (L57)\n- R9.53 Cap attempts at the factory\'s own bounds, then rebuild: one tagging pass per item ended a retry loop; an exhaustion receipt ended a re-post loop that spent about 75 candidates for 0 accepted. (period 2 lesson, not in the 57-row table)\n- R9.54 Rule at the plan stage on any step whose evidence the factory does not hold; never hold on it. The grader-evidence hold ran 66.4 hours for receipts the factory does not produce. (period 3 lesson, not in the 57-row table)\n- R9.55 Name the student destination and the full object inventory in the course profile before the first hand-off; when the close bar sits in another team\'s write corridor, file the fallback route in the same issue. (cause C1, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.56 Run the acceptance instrument from a pushed ref on a 200-question slice in the first week; read checks.py and timeback_reader.py before any structural write; carry the reader\'s known needs from the first publish. (cause C2, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.57 Give each course its own controller lease, lock locator and install root; measure the queue place before every paid step and write the wait into the ETA. (cause C3, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.58 Standing authority until the course is live, recorded once in a grant file every window reads; gates still run; no clock on the owner\'s words; an open decision blocks the publish step or carries a typed default. (cause C4, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.59 State progress only in the publication runbook\'s phase names; every local gate runs in shadow except the certification gate; a base-red suite gets an adjudication row, not a refusal. (cause C5, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.60 Make the re-pin a step of the item-campaign operator (plan, seal, execute, replay, re-pin) and keep the publisher\'s checkpoint in the repository so a re-pin republishes only what changed. (cause C6, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.61 Re-derive every quoted number from the live remote in the same turn; assert that a regenerated report changed; pair every hold with a \'landed so far\' line; point the event log at a receiver that exists. (cause C7, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.62 Every review finding returns with a deterministic, tested fix; a capped lane writes its report file first; PRs post ready-for-review; a small-course fixture keeps the suite under the CI cap; out-of-GitHub rounds are linked from the PR. (cause C8, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.63 Commit the publication runbook and a per-phase module inventory (exists or missing) to the course repository on intake day; plan from that inventory, never from an assumed pipeline. (cause C9, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.64 Run every unattended chain detached with progress visible from its checkpoint; refusal identity includes release and operator bytes with a retry budget; one install root per lane; free-space preflight before any sealed execute. (cause C10, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.65 Pilot one lesson, verify on the rendered course and one QC read, then scale; keep the operator\'s undo ready; a step that needs evidence the factory does not hold is ruled at the plan stage, not held. (cause C11, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.66 Write the content bar (exam shape of the mock, stimulus share, lesson row order, article format) into the course profile before generation, and show the owner one rendered lesson before the bank is generated. (cause C12, the one change for the next build)\n- R9.67 Every decision row carries a deadline and a default; every work order names a closing owner; superseded destinations close with a pointer the day the route changes. (cause C13, the one change for the next build)\n'

def patch(path: Path, anchor: str, block: str):
    s = path.read_text()
    assert s.count(anchor) == 1, (path, anchor[:60], s.count(anchor))
    path.write_text(s.replace(anchor, block + anchor))

if "apwh-build-20260804-20260921" not in (ROOT / "retro.html").read_text():
    patch(ROOT / "retro.html", '  <section id="humgeo-closeout-20260920">', RETRO)
if "apwh-lessons-20260921" not in (ROOT / "lessons.html").read_text():
    patch(ROOT / "lessons.html", '  <section id="publish-faster-20260920">', LESSONS.replace('\n    ', '\n  ').replace('\n      ', '\n    '))
spec = ROOT / "SPEC.md"
s = spec.read_text()
if "### R9." not in s:
    s = s.replace("\n## 2b. Where the build stands and what remains", "\n" + SPEC_ADD.rstrip("\n") + "\n\n## 2b. Where the build stands and what remains", 1)
    s = s.replace('"spec_version": "2026-09-20.45"', '"spec_version": "2026-09-21.46"')
    spec.write_text(s)
